# Deps only BepInEx (5.4.2350 = the 1.0 pack); built 2026-09-11. Client-only by design
# (BepInProcess valheim.exe): BepInEx SKIPS it on the dedicated server, so the server-side
# load-test is N/A - the remaining check is a real-client smoke test (install + Alt-click).
# Bumped 1.1.0 -> 1.2.0 on 2026-09-12: optional ExtraSlots 1.2.3 special-slot protection via
# its public API (NOT a required dependency; disabled by default).
FavoriteItems|1.2.0|FavoriteItems.dll|acc41c9304952623c2024700245d3b723c25272f1f923737d53626d8d4caf22c|optional|https://thunderstore.io/package/download/ronaldoniz/FavoriteItems/1.2.0/
# Unshamed (Azumatt): re-enables Steam achievements for players running mods. On 1.0 the achievement
# gate (Achievements.CanGetAchievements / IsCheatedAtAll) refuses achievements while Game.isModded is
# true (BepInEx sets it) — so every friend on our required client mods is blocked. Unshamed patches
# CanGetAchievements to ignore the four cheat/modded flags, WITHOUT touching the vanilla
# PlayerProfile.s_bypassCheatChecks switch (so spawned items still carry their cheated stamp normally,
# unlike the vanilla `yesiuseddevcommandsbutiwantmyachievementsanyway` command). CLIENT-SIDE ONLY: no
# ServerSync, nothing runs server-side, config is per-client (not server-synced) — so the server-side
# load test is low value (real gate = a client smoke test). optional: each friend who wants achievements
# installs it (ModSentry allows-but-doesn't-require). Deps only BepInEx. Added 2026-09-13, v1.0.4.
# Per-client config (Azumatt.Unshamed.cfg): set `Enable Retroactive = true` to grant already-earned
# achievements once on next load (default off). See client-modpack/INSTALL.md.
Unshamed|1.0.4|Unshamed.dll|c7a58666fa8c1efbfdea6e17e6b0ceee64baec0b823eeaf09249fa1bfaba3a1e|optional|https://thunderstore.io/package/download/Azumatt/Unshamed/1.0.4/
